{"name":"Duffel Bag","hex":"#464e3f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"duffel bag","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large, cylindrical, duffel cloth bag used to carry personal gear, especially by soldiers.","A smaller, cylindrical, cloth bag fashionable in the 1950s and 1960s."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/duffel_bag"}],"entries":[{"title":"Duffel bag","blocks":[{"text":"A duffel bag, duffle bag, or kit bag is a large bag made of either natural or synthetic fabric .\nIt typically has a rectangular base and a zippered opening at the top.\nTwo handles enable the bag to be carried, and a strap lets the user support the bag on the shoulders.\nIt may have wheels and possibly a telescopic handle.\nThe term covers a wide variety of types of bag."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Wriggle_House_-_Full-Grain_Genuine_leather_Holdall_Travel_Bag.jpg/330px-Wriggle_House_-_Full-Grain_Genuine_leather_Holdall_Travel_Bag.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duffel_bag"},{"title":"Duffel","blocks":[{"text":"Duffel is a municipality in the Belgian province of Antwerp."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Duffel%2C_monumentaal_pand1_foto1_2007-08-25_11.29.JPG/330px-Duffel%2C_monumentaal_pand1_foto1_2007-08-25_11.29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duffel"},{"title":"Bag","blocks":[{"text":"A bag, also known regionally as a sack or tote, is a common tool in the form of a floppy container, typically made of cloth, leather, bamboo, paper, or plastic. The use of bags predates recorded history, with the earliest bags being lengths of animal skin, cotton, or woven plant fibers, folded up at the edges and secured in that shape with strings of the same material. Bags can be used to carry items such as personal belongings, groceries, tools, and other objects. They come in various shapes and sizes, often equipped with handles or straps for easier carrying."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Bolsas-de-asa-plana-interior-bolsapubli.jpg/330px-Bolsas-de-asa-plana-interior-bolsapubli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bag"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Deora_Bodley%2C_the_youngest_person_aboard_Flight_93_on_11_September_2001%2C_has_her_gym_bag_on_display_from_the_wreckage_of_Flight_93_donated_by_her_family_at_the_CIA_Museum.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Deora_Bodley%2C_the_youngest_person_aboard_Flight_93_on_11_September_2001%2C_has_her_gym_bag_on_display_from_the_wreckage_of_Flight_93_donated_by_her_family_at_the_CIA_Museum.jpg/1280px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Deora_Bodley%2C_the_youngest_person_aboard_Flight_93_on_11_September_2001%2C_has_her_gym_bag_on_display_from_the_wreckage_of_Flight_93_donated_by_her_family_at_the_CIA_Museum.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gym bag recovered from the wreckage of Flight 93","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADeora_Bodley%2C_the_youngest_person_aboard_Flight_93_on_11_September_2001%2C_has_her_gym_bag_on_display_from_the_wreckage_of_Flight_93_donated_by_her_family_at_the_CIA_Museum.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Nationals_catcher_Jan_Gomes_%2810%29_gets_gear_out_of_bag_--_All-Pro_Reels_Ed_Sheahin_%2849571480293%29.jpg/500px-Nationals_catcher_Jan_Gomes_%2810%29_gets_gear_out_of_bag_--_All-Pro_Reels_Ed_Sheahin_%2849571480293%29.jpg?ut